-- title:
--   Places where jmath̄-j₀ vanishes count embedding classes
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $j_0$ be an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (the Lean `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`). Write $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N$ for [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldBar N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L111), the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, itself the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the divisor expansions attached to level $N$; let $\bar\jmath =$ `jBar N` be the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant viewed in $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N$. A place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is a valuation subring that contains the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is not all of $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N$ and is a principal ideal ring; $v.\mathrm{ord}$ denotes the associated normalised integer valuation. Let $S$ be a finite set of such places, and assume that a place $v$ lies in $S$ precisely when $v.\mathrm{ord}(\bar\jmath - j_0) > 0$. Then the cardinality of $S$ equals the number of elements of the quotient of [`ModularCurve.Emb N j₀`](def/ModularCurve_EMD.html#L22) — the set of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra homomorphisms $\psi : \overline{\mathbb Q}F_N \to$ `HahnSeries ℚ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` (Hahn series with rational exponents) satisfying $\psi(\bar\jmath) = j_0 + t$ — by the relation `SamePlace` on the underlying homomorphisms: $\psi \sim \psi'$ when there is one place $w$ and positive rationals $g, g'$ with $w.\mathrm{ord}(x)\, g = \operatorname{order}(\psi x)$ and $w.\mathrm{ord}(x)\, g' = \operatorname{order}(\psi' x)$ for all $x$.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the classical description of the points of $X_0(N)$ lying over a given $j$-invariant as classes of normalised Puiseux embeddings of the modular function field, the places being counted with multiplicity through the order of vanishing of $\bar\jmath - j_0$. It feeds the comparison [`ModularCurve.card_eq_natCard_moduliPoint_j_eq_of_EMD`](thm.html#ModularCurve.card_eq_natCard_moduliPoint_j_eq_of_EMD) between this count of places and the moduli-theoretic count of points with prescribed $j$-invariant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_card_eq_natCard_quot_samePlace_of_forall_mem_iff_pos_ord.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_EMD
